{"data":{"updated_timestamp":"12/11/2026 17:02:55","profile":{"player_id":"139581","last_updated":"12/11/2026 17:02","fullname":"Manal Chauhan","short_display_name":"M Chauhan","name":"Manal Chauhan","gender":"M","dob":"14/03/2008","date_of_death":null,"place_birth":"India","nationality_id":"4","nationality":"India","nationality_short_code":"IND","nick_name":null,"player_skill":{"id":"3","text":"All Rounder","role":"All Rounder"},"batting_style":{"id":"2","text":"Left Handed"},"bowling_style":{"id":"15","text":"Slow left-arm orthodox"},"writeup":"<p>Manal Chauhan is an all-action cricketer whose gritty determination and match-winning instincts have made him a vital presence in youth cricket. Chauhan is a gifted left-handed middle-order batter and a skillful slow left-arm orthodox bowler hailing from Morena, Madhya Pradesh.</p>\r\n<br />\r\n<p>His love for cricket took root during his early developmental years, where he developed a hardened competitive spirit and a deep work ethic facing tough opposition. He spent hours perfecting his left-handed technique, learning to rotate the strike through the middle overs and unleash powerful lofted strokes down the ground when acceleration was needed. Simultaneously, he honed his slow left-arm spin, learning how to deceive batters with subtle changes of trajectory, drift, and spin.</p>\r\n<br />\r\n<p>Throughout his domestic age-group campaigns, Manal built a formidable reputation across the junior circuit and invitational tournaments. Representing Madhya Pradesh across the Vijay Merchant Trophy, Vinoo Mankad Trophy, and Cooch Behar Trophy, he delivered a landmark season by accumulating 853 runs and taking 37 wickets. He repeatedly produced match-winning knocks and crucial bowling spells in high-pressure matches, earning a well-deserved call-up to the India Under-19 squad.</p>\r\n<br />\r\n<p>Manal announced his arrival on the international youth stage in dramatic fashion in July 2026 during the second Youth Test against Sri Lanka Under-19 in Galle. Batting first, India suffered a catastrophic collapse, losing both openers for zero within the opening overs. Arriving in the middle with the innings in tatters, Manal produced a masterclass in counter-attacking batting. He struck a stunning maiden youth Test century and converted it into an epic 150 runs off 244 balls, building a 155-run partnership with Kushagra Ojha to rescue the innings and propel India to an imposing total of 411, setting up a crushing victory.</p>\r\n<br />\r\n<p>His excellent form continued into September 2026, where he was selected for the India Under-19 squad to take on Australia Under-19 in Rajkot. Demonstrating his multi-dimensional value, Manal contributed with both bat and ball throughout the Youth ODI series - including a restrictive three-wicket haul in the final fixture - helping India complete an emphatic series sweep over the Australians.</p>","relation":null,"social_details":null,"trophy_cabinet":null,"majorteams":{"team":[{"id":"1163","active":"1","is_primary":"true","is_international":"1","text":"India Under-19"}]},"international_debut":null,"international_last_match":null,"stats":{"format":[{"comp_type_id":"21","comp_type":"Youth Test","debut":{"match_id":"271827","match_date":"20/07/2026","for":{"id":"1163","text":"India Under-19","short_name":"IND-U19"},"vs":{"id":"1165","text":"Sri Lanka Under-19","short_name":"SL-U19"},"venue":{"id":"131","text":"R.Premadasa Stadium, Colombo"}},"last_match":{"match_id":"270987","match_date":"05/10/2026","for":{"id":"1163","text":"India Under-19","short_name":"IND-U19"},"vs":{"id":"1154","text":"Australia Under-19","short_name":"AUS-U19"},"venue":{"id":"2738","text":"Narendra Modi Stadium Ground A, Motera, Ahmedabad"}},"rankings":{"bat":null,"bat_rating":"0","bowl":null,"bowl_rating":"0","allrounder":null,"allrounder_rating":"0","bat_rank_change":null,"bowl_rank_change":null,"allrounder_rank_change":null},"overall":{"batting_record":{"matches":"3","innings":"4","not_o